# pcloud-rs @VERSION@ for @PLATFORM@/@ARCH@

This is a native binary package candidate. Its `root/` directory mirrors the
filesystem paths to install. Verify both the adjacent archive checksum and
`MANIFEST.sha256` before copying any payload as root.

The candidate does not create a service account or enable the daemon. Follow
the platform instructions shipped under `root/usr/local/share/doc/pcloud-rs/`
to create the dedicated `pcloudd` identity, configure an owner-only credential
file, validate the service definition, and enable it explicitly.

Kernel mounting is deliberately unavailable on illumos and Oracle Solaris;
the CLI, daemon IPC, remote transfer, copy, and sharing surfaces remain usable.
DragonFly includes its native FUSE mount adapter, subject to a successful
release-commit live-mount gate.
